  "notes": "A formal term for the deliberate termination of a pregnancy, carrying a legal and clinical tone. In everyday speech ⟦{中絶|ちゅうぜつ}→中絶：16292_chuuzetsu⟧, or ⟦{人工|じんこう}→人工：11573_jinkou⟧⟦{妊娠|にんしん}→妊娠：12227_ninshin⟧⟦{中絶|ちゅうぜつ}→中絶：16292_chuuzetsu⟧, is far more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {堕胎|だたい}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to have or perform an abortion\n- {堕胎|だたい}{罪|ざい}: the crime of illegal abortion\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{中絶|ちゅうぜつ}→中絶：16292_chuuzetsu⟧: termination — the ordinary, everyday word\n- {流産|りゅうざん}: miscarriage — spontaneous, not deliberate",
